# Expose the ADAU1860 codec on the ACP card as a separate PulseAudio sink.
#
# Card 1 has two PCM playback devices:
#   hw:1,0 -> NAU8822 codec (analog speakers/headphones)
#   hw:1,1 -> ADAU1860 codec (I2S link via Versal mux to I2S_BT)
#
# PulseAudio's auto-detected ALSA card profile only binds the first codec PCM,
# so without this the ADAU1860 link is invisible to applications. Loading it
# explicitly gives the user a second selectable sink in the rave-menu
# Setup Audio screen and to Chromium.
#
# Pin the sink to 48 kHz s16le stereo. The downstream EVAL-ADAU1860 codec
# is clocked from a 24.576 MHz crystal whose only integer relationship is
# to the 48 kHz family (24.576 MHz / 512 = 48 kHz). Letting PulseAudio
# auto-pick 44.1 kHz feeds the codec a non-integer-related BCLK and the
# internal datapath - configured for 48 kHz by the Lark Studio project -
# resamples with the wrong ratio, producing audible pitch/speed drift and
# tinny/robotic artefacts. Resample inside PA (cheap, high quality with
# default speex-float-1) rather than fighting the codec's clock tree.
#
# NOTE: load-module statements must live on a single line - default.pa
# does not honour backslash continuations.

load-module module-alsa-sink device=hw:1,1 rate=48000 format=s16le channels=2 sink_name=acp_versal_i2s sink_properties=device.description="ADAU1860\ (Versal\ I2S)"
